Z||000000||gkozlov||07-27-2000||08:45 PM||||OK to prep my question I am currently running an Alpine 7835 headunit, Pioneer 6X9's up front and Pioneer 4X6's in the sail panels. I have an Altec Lansing computer sub behind the passenger side seat.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Dscf0011.jpg">  <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Mvc-213s.jpg">  <P>I just bought a Rock Fosgate 8" sub. and a Jensen 600 watt 6 channel amp. I chose this amp because I didnt want mount and install multiple amps. <P>I've been reading about alot about the installs you guys have done. Impressive. But due to my small income (military) I have to make do and often cut corners.<P>TheFiero64 has given me an idea <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/004905.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/004905.html</A>  . Could I buy some 8 inch PVC pipe and make my own "Bazooka" tube?  If so how long would the tube have to be? I would like to mount it under the dash where the factory sub would go. Could I do the same for my Altec Lansing sub? Put in a tube that is. How long would that 6.5 inch tube have to be? That would stay behind the seat though. It would save me a ton of space. <BR><p>[This message has been edited by gkozlov (edited 07-27-2000).]||||reg||1
